{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/181307-compacts-conspiracies-as-mystery-cults","id":181307,"title":"Compacts/Conspiracies as Mystery Cults","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-26T15:56:57-07:00","id":181307,"title":"Compacts/Conspiracies as Mystery Cults","content":"When I first cracked open the GMC update and saw the Mystery Cult merit, my first thought was that the Merit was a stealth update of a Compact or Conspiracy's Status.<br /> <br /> Most Compacts can fit the bulk of their benefits into 3 dots of Mystery Cult, which might also hold true for Conspiracies (haven't checked). However, they need to grant 1 more dot of Merits at the 2nd dot to match Status entirely.<br /> <br /> For example, here is Network Zero as a Mystery Cult:<br /> <br /> \u2022 : Free specialty in either Crafts or Expression<br /> \u2022\u2022 : Fame \u2022 (Fame \u2022\u2022 if you go with giving them a 2-dot Merit at Mystery Cult \u2022\u2022)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022: Encyclopedic Knowledge (Occult)<br /> <br /> Or the Union:<br /> <br /> \u2022 : Free specialty in either Streetwise or Politics<br /> \u2022\u2022 : Contacts (Union) \u2022 (Contacts (Union) \u2022\u2022 if you go with giving them a 2-dot Merit at Mystery Cult \u2022\u2022)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022: Resources \u2022\u2022<br /> <br /> Or the Loyalists of Thule:<br /> <br /> \u2022 : +1 WP regained if you risk Willpower on an Occult or Academics rolls and succeed (roughly equal to a 1-dot merit.)<br /> \u2022\u2022 : Mentor \u2022 (Mentor \u2022\u2022 if you go with giving them a 2-dot Merit at Mystery Cult \u2022\u2022)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022: Contacts \u2022\u2022 (Drat. So close; Loyalists get 3 dots from Status.)<br /> <br /> Or, to go with a Conspiracy, the Cainite Heresy:<br /> <br /> \u2022 : Rites of Denial \u2022<br /> \u2022\u2022 : Danger Sense (Full Danger Sense vs. Vampires, halved vs. everyone else; I'd call that a fair 1 to 2 dot merit.)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022: Mentor \u2022\u2022 (Just like the Loyalists, they have a 3 dot merit at Status 5.)<br /> <br /> Or, one of my favorites, VASCU:<br /> <br /> \u2022 : Teleinformatics \u2022<br /> \u2022\u2022 : Status (FBI) \u2022 (This is what they actually get in Slashers; I'd personally hand them Status (FBI) \u2022\u2022, because I am anal about patterns)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022: Inspiring (Hmm... I'm starting to think Conspiracies get a 3-dot merit at Status 5.)<br /> <br /> And one of the new Conspiracies for good measure, Faithful of Shulpae:<br /> <br /> \u2022 : Anthropophagy \u2022<br /> \u2022\u2022 : Safehouse \u2022 (Safehouse \u2022\u2022 if you want to follow the blablabla you get the drift)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022: 2 dots in Supernatural Merits (They get <i>4</i>. <i>4</i> dots in Supernatural Merits. 3 dots is fair, as far as I see it.)<br /> <br /> So, my little metric is:<br /> <br /> \u2022 Use Mystery Cult in place of Status.<br /> \u2022 Hunter Mystery Cults go up to 3 dots; you can totally expand them past that point if you want, though.<br /> \u2022 Hunters get a two-dot Merit at Mystery Cult \u2022\u2022.<br /> \u2022 Conspiracies get a three-dot Merit at Mystery Cult \u2022\u2022\u2022.<br /> \u2022 Conspiracies get one dot of their Endowment at Mystery Cult \u2022.<br /> \u2022 If you want the social benefits, buy a dot or two of the actual Status merit for your Compact/Conspiracy.<br /> \u2022 If you are making a game where your group founds a Compact from their Cell, you've got a nice guideline for their Mystery Cult merit.<br /> <br /> So, while this might result in some Compacts and Conspiracies that are more or less powerful than before... I'm fine with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-26T16:00:27-07:00","id":181323,"title":"","content":"Almost forgot another little note:<br /> <br /> The boost to Mystery Cult is to make up for the fact that Hunters are the only major splat updated to GMC stuck with 7 merit dots at character creation. With this set-up, Compacts get a hidden 1-dot boost, while Conspiracies get a hidden 2-dot boost.<br /> <br /> So you get a:<br /> <br /> Mortals: 7<br /> Compacts: 8<br /> Conspiracies: 9<br /> Supernaturals: 10<br /> <br /> Scale. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}